      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Osteoarthritis represents a massive and rapidly increasing burden on our society and the NHS. Current treatments are limited in efficacy and have significant toxicities. A conference was organised in conjunction with the British Society of Rheumatology with the aim of updating frontline clinicians and researchers on the size and causes of this problem, with a focus on modern management."},
